 "title": "Biofilm Formation and Characterization in Bacteria",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the formation and characterization of biofilms in bacteria. E. coli, a type of bacteria, grows into a biofilm, which has properties such as curli amyloid fibers and extracellular matrix. Biofilms influence the presence of agar, matrix, and nutrients. The biofilm's composition includes curli fibers, which interact with Direct Red and Nile Red. Biofilms are characterized using methods such as SDS-PAGE, BioRad, Sigma, and Thioflavin T. Curli amyloid fibers, a component of biofilms, are analyzed using Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy and bind to Thioflavin T.",
